# Runtime state, not source. BASE_STATE is /workspace/comfy-base/state on a pod; running base.sh from the
# repo puts it here instead, and a `git add .` would otherwise sweep a run's logs into a commit.
state/
# the base's own toolchain when installed beside the checkout (uv's python, the venv)
python/
# per-run tool output: pod logs, pins, canvas snapshots and review renders, wherever a _build/ sits
**/_build/podruns/
**/_build/pins/
**/_build/snapshots/
**/_build/review.svg
**/_build/review-focus.svg
# python and pytest leavings
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
# the Mac
.DS_Store
# the MCP client configuration `podctl mcp <machine>` writes: it names ONE machine and one operator's paths,
# so it is per-checkout, never committed. Upstream's own `comfy skills install` handles a LOCAL ComfyUI and
# writes at user scope; this file is only for a machine the base provisioned.
.mcp.json
# the shared ComfyUI testbed: an upstream clone plus its packs and venv, provisioned by ./testbed.sh and
# reproducible from it. Several GB, none of it ours.
/testbed/
# the local testbed server's pid, log and port files
.testbed-server.*
